# Agent routing (system wrapper)

**Repo entry:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). **Do not** treat [docs/roadmap.md](../../docs/roadmap.md) as the queue.

**Hard gates:** [kanban-card-gates.mdc](kanban-card-gates.mdc) — kanban card required for implementation; valid frontmatter `labels` required.

## User mode

| Mode | Work source | Code / cards |
| ---- | ----------- | ------------ |
| **Agent** | Card named + **agent verb** — `implement`, `update`, `plan approved`, `review and update`, `spawn`, `Done`, `QA complete`, `epic complete`, … | [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md); [kanban-card-gates.mdc](kanban-card-gates.mdc) §2 |
| **Ask-only** | `review …` only, bare `@path`, **`Inquire @card`**, no card, or no agent verb | Read-only — no file edits |
| **Plan (chat-only)** | **`Plan @card`** alone | Plan Mode — discuss in chat; no card edits until approval |

## Turn lifecycle

```text
START → agent-triage/SKILL.md (classify; card + label + prompt-verb gate incl. Plan/Inquire modes; one scoped kanban-*-cards.mdc; §1b on failure signals only)
WORK  → card Product + Tests + Docs → prior lessons gate (feature/bug/agent/commit-issue)
        → Decisions / Corrective Action → implement
        → Review QA fix: **QA follow-up** + refresh Feature Areas / Product / Tests / Docs
VERIFY → ruff E501 on touched `.py`/`.pyi` before handoff; targeted pytest; pre-commit-pytest.sh before Review/commit
DONE  → user QA-complete / Done signal → agent moves to done/ + lessons + forward feedback
        **only** for feature / bug / agent / commit-issue (Signature: card-done-agent-move-qa-complete)
        → user epic complete → § Epic audit on anchor + **`### Epic summary`** (Signature:
        governance-epic-completion-audit, governance-epic-completion-summary)
        → user archive group complete → § Archive group on anchor + **`### Initiative summary`**
        (Signature: governance-archive-group-batch, governance-epic-completion-summary)
        → top-3 forward feedback in chat before handoff; inquiry Done: move only — no lessons
        → build_lessons_index.py when lessons ran; build_forward_feedback_index.py when lessons
        ran (Signature: `forward-feedback-card-done-ingest`); curate feature-areas lesson_* when applicable
END   → agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md + handoff block
```

**Implementation / fix / refactor:** edit **≥1** `.cursor/skills/*` and **≥1** `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` before handoff (different learnings — skill = workflow, rule = constraint).

## Kanban card type (read `labels` in frontmatter)

| Label | Rule | Agent plan section |
| ----- | ---- | ------------------ |
| `feature` | [kanban-feature-cards.mdc](kanban-feature-cards.mdc) | **Decisions** |
| `bug` | [kanban-bug-cards.mdc](kanban-bug-cards.mdc) | **Corrective Action** (not Decisions) |
| `commit-issue` | [kanban-commit-issue-cards.mdc](kanban-commit-issue-cards.mdc) | **Review** → Root Cause + Corrective Action; implement after user approval |
| `inquiry` | [kanban-inquiry-cards.mdc](kanban-inquiry-cards.mdc) | **Response** after `update`; **`Inquire @card`** + Ask Mode — Signature: `kanban-cursor-mode-gates` |
| `plan` | [kanban-plan-cards.mdc](kanban-plan-cards.mdc) | **Recommendation** after approval; **`Plan @card`** + Plan Mode — Signature: `kanban-cursor-mode-gates` |
| `agent` | [kanban-agent-cards.mdc](kanban-agent-cards.mdc) | **Decisions**; user **Description** + **Feature Area** |
| **Invalid** (missing / `[]` / unknown) | [kanban-card-gates.mdc](kanban-card-gates.mdc) | **Stop** — user must fix `labels` |

Resolve **Feature Areas** (or agent card **Feature Area**) → **Product Paths** + **Product Methods**
+ **Tests** + **Docs** via [docs/feature-areas.yaml](../../docs/feature-areas.yaml) before `in-progress`.

## Code style (Python)

All agent edits to `.py` / `.pyi` files must keep lines ≤ **100** characters (`pyproject.toml`
`line-length = 100`). **Before handoff** on implementation turns, run
`.venv/bin/ruff check --select E501` on every touched path — Signature: `ruff-e501-line-length`.
Pre-commit ruff is hook 1; E501 failures must not reach commit. Wrap strings, split imports,
break call chains while editing — not only after hook failure.

